{"1384":["<h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">GEOMETRY — 1. ANGLE RULES IN TRIANGLES</h4><h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">(PICTURE CARDS)</h4><p style=\"color:#d32f2f;font-size:1.20em;font-weight:700\">LOOK AT THE PICTURE · LEARN THE ONE-LINE RULE · CHECK THE EXAMPLE</p><i data-k=\"0\"></i><i data-k=\"1\"></i><i data-k=\"2\"></i><i data-k=\"3\"></i><i data-k=\"4\"></i><i data-k=\"5\"></i><i data-k=\"6\"></i><i data-k=\"7\"></i><i data-k=\"8\"></i>",[["img/refp/geometry-0.webp",443,7602,0,443,463,245],["img/refp/geometry-0.webp",443,7602,469,442,463,245],["img/refp/geometry-0.webp",443,7602,938,443,463,245],["img/refp/geometry-0.webp",443,7602,1407,443,489,245],["img/refp/geometry-0.webp",443,7602,1902,442,489,245],["img/refp/geometry-0.webp",443,7602,2397,443,489,245],["img/refp/geometry-0.webp",443,7602,2892,443,463,245],["img/refp/geometry-0.webp",443,7602,3361,442,463,245],["img/refp/geometry-0.webp",443,7602,3830,443,463,245]]],"1385":["<h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">GEOMETRY — 2. MORE ANGLE RULES (BISECTORS, ALTITUDES, POLYGONS)</h4><p style=\"color:#d32f2f;font-size:1.20em;font-weight:700\">RULES 10–18 · EVERY PICTURE IS DRAWN TO EXACT GEOMETRY</p><i data-k=\"0\"></i><i data-k=\"1\"></i><i data-k=\"2\"></i><i data-k=\"3\"></i><i data-k=\"4\"></i><i data-k=\"5\"></i><i data-k=\"6\"></i><i data-k=\"7\"></i><i data-k=\"8\"></i>",[["img/refp/geometry-0.webp",443,7602,4299,443,463,245],["img/refp/geometry-0.webp",443,7602,4768,443,463,245],["img/refp/geometry-0.webp",443,7602,5237,442,463,245],["img/refp/geometry-0.webp",443,7602,5706,443,463,245],["img/refp/geometry-0.webp",443,7602,6175,443,463,245],["img/refp/geometry-0.webp",443,7602,6644,442,463,245],["img/refp/geometry-0.webp",443,7602,7113,443,489,245],["img/refp/geometry-1.webp",443,984,0,443,489,245],["img/refp/geometry-1.webp",443,984,495,442,489,245]]],"1386":["<h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">GEOMETRY — 3. LINES, TRIANGLES &amp;</h4><h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">PYTHAGORAS</h4><p style=\"color:#d32f2f;font-size:1.11em;font-weight:700\">CONCEPTS AND FORMULA RULES</p><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f4f8fc;border-color:#1565c0\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#1565c0;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.14em;font-weight:700;background:#1565c0;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Lines &amp; angles</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\" style=\"--hc:#1565c0\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Complementary</td><td>= sum = 90°</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Supplementary</td><td>= sum = 180°</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Angles at a point</td><td>= sum = 360°</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Vertically opposite</td><td>= equal</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style=\"color:#8a6100\">Parallel lines cut by a transversal:</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\" style=\"--hc:#1565c0\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Corresponding</td><td>= equal (F shape)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Alternate interior</td><td>= equal (Z shape)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Co-interior (same</p><p>= sum = 180° (C/U shape)</p><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">side)</p></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f6f9f6;border-color:#2e7d32\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#2e7d32;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.14em;font-weight:700;background:#2e7d32;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Types of triangles</p><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Equilateral = <sup>3 sides equal, each angle</sup></p><p>60°</p><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Isosceles = <sup>2 sides equal → base angles</sup></p><p>equal</p><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Scalene = all sides &amp; angles different</p><p><span style=\"color:#1a3a8f\"><b>Acute / right / obtuse</b></span> = largest angle &lt; / = / &gt; 90°</p><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Test with sides (c = <sup>c² &lt; a² + b² acute · = right ·</sup> longest) &gt; obtuse</p><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Exterior angle = <sup>= sum of 2 opposite interior</sup></p><p>angles</p></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#fcf5f5;border-color:#c62828\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#c62828;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.14em;font-weight:700;background:#c62828;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Pythagoras &amp; triples</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\" style=\"--hc:#c62828\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Right triangle</td><td>= <sup>a² + b² = c² (c =</sup> hypotenuse)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Triples</td><td>= 3-4-5 · 5-12-13 · 8-15-17</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">More triples</td><td>= 7-24-25 · 9-40-41 · 20-21-29</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Multiples work</td><td>= 6-8-10 · 9-12-15 · 15-20-25</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">30-60-90 sides</td><td>= 1 : √3 : 2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">45-45-90 sides</td><td>= 1 : 1 : √2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Equilateral height</td><td>= (√3/2) a</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#fef8f4;border-color:#ef6c00\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#ef6c00;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.14em;font-weight:700;background:#ef6c00;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Area of a triangle</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\" style=\"--hc:#944300\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Base &amp; height</td><td>= ½ × b × h</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Two sides &amp; angle</td><td>= ½ ab sin C</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Heron (3 sides)</td><td>= <sup>√[s(s − a)(s − b)(s − c)], s</sup> = (a + b + c)/2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Equilateral</td><td>= (√3/4) a²</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Right triangle</td><td>= ½ × leg₁ × leg₂</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Inradius r</td><td>= Area / s</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Circumradius R</td><td>= abc / (4 × Area)</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f8f5fa;border-color:#6a1b9a\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#6a1b9a;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.14em;font-weight:700;background:#6a1b9a;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Centres of a triangle</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\" style=\"--hc:#6a1b9a\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Centroid G</td><td>= <sup>medians meet · divides</sup> each 2 : 1</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Incentre I</td><td>= <sup>angle bisectors meet ·</sup> centre of incircle</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Circumcentre O</td><td>= <sup>perpendicular bisectors</sup> meet · OA = OB = OC = R</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Orthocentre H</td><td>= altitudes meet</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Right triangle</td><td>= <sup>O = midpoint of</sup> hypotenuse, R = c/2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Equilateral</td><td>= <sup>all four centres coincide · R</sup> = 2r</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f4f9fa;border-color:#00838f\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#00838f;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.14em;font-weight:700;background:#00838f;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Similar &amp; congruent</p><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Similar (AA, SAS,</p><p>= same shape, sides in ratio k</p><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">SSS)</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\" style=\"--hc:#00838f\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Area ratio</td><td>= k² (squares of sides)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Volume ratio</td><td>= k³</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Basic proportionality</td><td>= <sup>line ∥ base cuts sides in</sup> same ratio</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Angle bisector</p><p>= BD/DC = AB/AC</p><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">theorem</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\" style=\"--hc:#00838f\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Congruent tests</td><td>= SSS, SAS, ASA, AAS, RHS</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>",[]],"1387":["<h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">GEOMETRY — 4. POLYGONS, RECTANGLES,</h4><h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">CIRCLES, BOXES &amp; SOLIDS</h4><p style=\"color:#d32f2f;font-size:1.11em;font-weight:700\">CONCEPTS AND FORMULA RULES</p><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f4f8fc;border-color:#1565c0\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#1565c0;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.14em;font-weight:700;background:#1565c0;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Polygons (n sides)</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\" style=\"--hc:#1565c0\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Interior angle sum</td><td>= (n − 2) × 180°</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Each interior</p><p>= (n − 2) × 180° / n</p><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">(regular)</p><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Each exterior</p><p>= 360° / n</p><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">(regular)</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\" style=\"--hc:#1565c0\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Sides from exterior</td><td>= n = 360° / exterior</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Number of diagonals = n(n − 3) / 2</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\" style=\"--hc:#1565c0\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Interior + exterior</td><td>= = 180° at each vertex</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Examples</td><td>pentagon 540° (108° each) · hexagon 720° (120°) · = octagon 1080° (135°)</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f6f9f6;border-color:#2e7d32\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#2e7d32;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.14em;font-weight:700;background:#2e7d32;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Rectangle, square &amp; quadrilaterals</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\" style=\"--hc:#2e7d32\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Rectangle area</td><td>= l × b</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Rectangle perimeter = 2(l + b)</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\" style=\"--hc:#2e7d32\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Rectangle diagonal</td><td>= √(l² + b²)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Square</td><td>= <sup>area a² · perimeter 4a ·</sup> diagonal a√2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Parallelogram</td><td>= <sup>base × height · opposite</sup> angles equal</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Rhombus</td><td>= <sup>½ d₁d₂ · side = ½√(d₁² +</sup> d₂²)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Trapezium</td><td>= ½ (a + b) × h</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Cyclic quadrilateral</td><td>= opposite angles add to 180°</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#fcf5f5;border-color:#c62828\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#c62828;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.14em;font-weight:700;background:#c62828;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Circle</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\" style=\"--hc:#c62828\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Circumference</td><td>= 2πr = πd</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Area</td><td>= πr²</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Arc length</td><td>= <sup>rθ (θ in rad) = (θ/360°) ×</sup> 2πr</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Sector area</td><td>= ½ r²θ = (θ/360°) × πr²</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Angle at centre</td><td>= <sup>= 2 × angle at</sup> circumference</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Angle in a semicircle = 90°</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\" style=\"--hc:#c62828\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Same segment</td><td>= angles are equal</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Tangent</td><td>= <sup>□ radius · length = √(d² −</sup> r²)</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#fef8f4;border-color:#ef6c00\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#ef6c00;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.14em;font-weight:700;background:#ef6c00;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Box (cuboid), cube &amp; solids</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\" style=\"--hc:#944300\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Cuboid volume</td><td>= l × b × h</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Cuboid total surface</td><td>= 2(lb + bh + hl)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Cuboid side walls</td><td>= 2h(l + b)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Box diagonal</td><td>= √(l² + b² + h²)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Cube</td><td>= <sup>V = a³ · TSA = 6a² ·</sup> diagonal a√3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Cylinder</td><td>= <sup>V = πr²h · CSA 2πrh · TSA</sup> 2πr(r + h)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Cone</td><td>= <sup>V = ⅓πr²h · slant l = √(r² +</sup> h²) · CSA πrl</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Sphere / hemisphere = V = ⁴⁄₃πr³ · 4πr² / ⅔πr³ · 3πr²</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\" style=\"--hc:#944300\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Prism / pyramid</td><td>= <sup>V = base area × h / ⅓ ×</sup> base area × h</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>",[]],"1388":["<h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">GEOMETRY — SUM OF INTERIOR ANGLES OF</h4><h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">POLYGONS</h4><p style=\"color:#d32f2f;font-weight:700\">TRIANGLE TO DODECAGON · (n − 2) × 180°</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\" style=\"--hc:#1b2a4a\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Sum of interior angles No. Polygon Sides n (n − 2) × 180°</th><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Each interior (regular)</th><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Each exterior 360°/n</th><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Diagonals n(n−3)/2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 3 (3 − 2) × 180° = <span style=\"color:#c62828\"><b>180°</b></span> Triangle</td><td data-h=\"Each interior (regular)\">60°</td><td data-h=\"Each exterior 360°/n\">120°</td><td data-h=\"Diagonals n(n−3)/2\">0</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">2 4 (4 − 2) × 180° = <span style=\"color:#c62828\"><b>360°</b></span> Quadrilateral</td><td data-h=\"Each interior (regular)\">90°</td><td data-h=\"Each exterior 360°/n\">90°</td><td data-h=\"Diagonals n(n−3)/2\">2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">3 5 (5 − 2) × 180° = <span style=\"color:#c62828\"><b>540°</b></span> Pentagon</td><td data-h=\"Each interior (regular)\">108°</td><td data-h=\"Each exterior 360°/n\">72°</td><td data-h=\"Diagonals n(n−3)/2\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">4 6 (6 − 2) × 180° = <span style=\"color:#c62828\"><b>720°</b></span> Hexagon</td><td data-h=\"Each interior (regular)\">120°</td><td data-h=\"Each exterior 360°/n\">60°</td><td data-h=\"Diagonals n(n−3)/2\">9</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">5 7 (7 − 2) × 180° = <span style=\"color:#c62828\"><b>900°</b></span> Heptagon</td><td data-h=\"Each interior (regular)\">128.57° (900/7°)</td><td data-h=\"Each exterior 360°/n\">51.43° (360/7°)</td><td data-h=\"Diagonals n(n−3)/2\">14</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">6 8 (8 − 2) × 180° = <span style=\"color:#c62828\"><b>1080°</b></span> Octagon</td><td data-h=\"Each interior (regular)\">135°</td><td data-h=\"Each exterior 360°/n\">45°</td><td data-h=\"Diagonals n(n−3)/2\">20</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">7 9 (9 − 2) × 180° = <span style=\"color:#c62828\"><b>1260°</b></span> Nonagon</td><td data-h=\"Each interior (regular)\">140°</td><td data-h=\"Each exterior 360°/n\">40°</td><td data-h=\"Diagonals n(n−3)/2\">27</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">8 10 (10 − 2) × 180° = <span style=\"color:#c62828\"><b>1440°</b></span> Decagon</td><td data-h=\"Each interior (regular)\">144°</td><td data-h=\"Each exterior 360°/n\">36°</td><td data-h=\"Diagonals n(n−3)/2\">35</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">9 11 (11 − 2) × 180° = <span style=\"color:#c62828\"><b>1620°</b></span> Hendecagon</td><td data-h=\"Each interior (regular)\">147.27° (1620/11°)</td><td data-h=\"Each exterior 360°/n\">32.73° (360/11°)</td><td data-h=\"Diagonals n(n−3)/2\">44</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">10 12 (12 − 2) × 180° = <span style=\"color:#c62828\"><b>1800°</b></span> Dodecagon</td><td data-h=\"Each interior (regular)\">150°</td><td data-h=\"Each exterior 360°/n\">30°</td><td data-h=\"Diagonals n(n−3)/2\">54</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><b>Why (n − 2) × 180°?</b> From one corner you can draw lines to every other corner and split the polygon into <b>n − 2</b> <b>triangles</b>; each triangle has 180°. Hexagon: 4 triangles → 4 × 180° = 720°. <b>Exterior angles of any convex</b> <b>polygon always add to 360°</b>, so each exterior angle of a regular polygon is 360°/n, and interior + exterior = 180° at every corner.</p><p style=\"color:#1b5e20\"><b>Quick checks:</b> each interior angle 150° → exterior 30° → n = 360/30 = 12 (dodecagon) · a polygon with 9 diagonals</p><p style=\"color:#1b5e20\">→ n(n − 3)/2 = 9 → n = 6 (hexagon) · interior sum 1440° → n − 2 = 8 → n = 10 (decagon).</p>",[]],"1389":["<h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">GEOMETRY — 5. SOLVED SUMS (TRIANGLES,</h4><h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">RECTANGLES, CIRCLES, BOXES)</h4><p style=\"color:#d32f2f;font-size:1.14em;font-weight:700\">44 SUMS · COVER THE ANSWER, TRY FIRST, THEN CHECK</p><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f4f8fc;border-color:#1565c0\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#1565c0;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.17em;font-weight:700;background:#1565c0;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Angles &amp; triangles</p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">1.</span> Two angles of a triangle are 47° and 68°. Third angle?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 180 − 47 − 68 <b>= 65°</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">2.</span> Angles are in ratio 2 : 3 : 4. Largest angle?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 9 parts = 180° → 1 part 20° <b>= 80°</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">3.</span> Exterior angle 120°, one opposite interior angle 50°. Other?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 120 − 50 <b>= 70°</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">4.</span> Isosceles triangle, apex 50°. Each base angle?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> (180 − 50)/2 <b>= 65°</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">5.</span> Find x in your puzzle (base angles 30°, 25°).</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> angle at crossing = 180 − 30 − 25 <b>= 125°</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">6.</span> Bisectors of B and C meet at I; A = 80°. ∠BIC?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 90 + 80/2 <b>= 130°</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">7.</span> External bisectors of B, C meet; A = 80°. Angle there?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 90 − 80/2 <b>= 50°</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">8.</span> Altitudes from B and C meet at H; A = 65°. ∠BHC?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 180 − 65 <b>= 115°</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">9.</span> Dart: angles 35°, 45°, 30° at the three outer corners. x?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 35 + 45 + 30 <b>= 110°</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">10.</span> Supplement of 3 times an angle is 60°. The angle?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 3x = 120 <b>= 40°</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">11.</span> Parallel lines: co-interior angles are x and 2x. x?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 3x = 180 <b>= 60°</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">12.</span> Sides 4 and 9: possible third sides (whole numbers)?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 5 &lt; c &lt; 13 → 6 … 12 <b>= 7 values</b></p></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#fcf5f5;border-color:#c62828\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#c62828;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.17em;font-weight:700;background:#c62828;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Pythagoras &amp; area</p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">13.</span> Legs 9 and 12. Hypotenuse?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> √(81 + 144) = √225 <b>= 15</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">14.</span> Ladder 13 m, foot 5 m from wall. Height reached?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> √(169 − 25) <b>= 12 m</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">15.</span> Is 7, 10, 12 acute, right or obtuse?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 144 vs 49 + 100 = 149 <b>= acute</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">16.</span> Area of triangle with sides 13, 14, 15 (Heron).</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> s = 21, √(21·8·7·6) = √7056 <b>= 84</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">17.</span> Equilateral triangle side 6. Area?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> (√3/4) × 36 <b>= 9√3 ≈ 15.59</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">18.</span> Two sides 8, 10 with 30° between them. Area?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> ½ × 8 × 10 × sin 30° <b>= 20</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">19.</span> Right triangle legs 6, 8. Circumradius R?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> hyp = 10 → R = 10/2 <b>= 5</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">20.</span> Right triangle 6-8-10. Inradius r?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> Area 24, s = 12 → 24/12 <b>= 2</b></p></div>",[]],"1390":["<h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">GEOMETRY — 6. SOLVED SUMS (continued)</h4><p style=\"color:#d32f2f;font-size:1.14em;font-weight:700\">POLYGONS · RECTANGLES · CIRCLES · BOXES &amp; SOLIDS</p><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f8f5fa;border-color:#6a1b9a\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#6a1b9a;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.17em;font-weight:700;background:#6a1b9a;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Polygons</p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">21.</span> Interior angle sum of an octagon?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> (8 − 2) × 180 <b>= 1080°</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">22.</span> Each exterior angle of a regular polygon is 24°. Sides?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 360/24 <b>= 15</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">23.</span> Each interior angle 150°. Number of sides?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> exterior 30° → 360/30 <b>= 12</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">24.</span> Diagonals of a decagon?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 10 × 7 / 2 <b>= 35</b></p></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f6f9f6;border-color:#2e7d32\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#2e7d32;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.17em;font-weight:700;background:#2e7d32;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Rectangles &amp; quadrilaterals</p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">25.</span> Rectangle 12 m × 5 m: area, perimeter, diagonal?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 60 · 2(17) · √(144 + 25) <b>= 60 m², 34 m, 13 m</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">26.</span> Rectangle perimeter 46 cm, length 15 cm. Area?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> b = 23 − 15 = 8 → 15 × 8 <b>= 120 cm²</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">27.</span> Square diagonal 10√2 cm. Area?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> side 10 → 10² <b>= 100 cm²</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">28.</span> Rhombus diagonals 16 and 12. Area and side?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> ½ × 16 × 12 · ½√(256 + 144) <b>= 96, side 10</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">29.</span> Trapezium parallel sides 10, 6, height 4. Area?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> ½ (10 + 6) × 4 <b>= 32</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">30.</span> Room 5 m × 4 m tiled with 0.5 m square tiles. Tiles?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 20 / 0.25 <b>= 80</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">31.</span> Cyclic quadrilateral: one angle 75°. Opposite angle?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 180 − 75 <b>= 105°</b></p></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f4f9fa;border-color:#00838f\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#00838f;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.17em;font-weight:700;background:#00838f;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Circles</p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">32.</span> Circle radius 7 cm (π = 22/7): area and circumference?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 22/7 × 49 · 2 × 22/7 × 7 <b>= 154 cm², 44 cm</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">33.</span> Sector of radius 6, angle 60°. Arc length?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> (60/360) × 2π × 6 <b>= 2π ≈ 6.28</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">34.</span> Angle at circumference 35° on arc AB. Angle at centre?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 2 × 35 <b>= 70°</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">35.</span> Tangent from a point 13 cm from centre, r = 5. Length?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> √(169 − 25) <b>= 12 cm</b></p></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#fef8f4;border-color:#ef6c00\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#ef6c00;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.17em;font-weight:700;background:#ef6c00;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Boxes &amp; solids</p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">36.</span> Box 10 × 6 × 4 cm: volume, surface, diagonal?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 240 · 2(60 + 24 + 40) · √(100 + 36 + 16) <b>= 240 cm³,</b> 248 cm², √152 ≈ 12.33 cm</p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">37.</span> Tank 2 m × 1.5 m × 1 m. Litres of water?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 3 m³ × 1000 <b>= 3000 L</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">38.</span> Cube volume 343 cm³. Surface area?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> side 7 → 6 × 49 <b>= 294 cm²</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">39.</span> Cube side doubled. Volume becomes?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> (2a)³ = 8a³ <b>= 8 times</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">40.</span> Cylinder r = 7, h = 10 (π = 22/7). Volume?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 22/7 × 49 × 10 <b>= 1540</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">41.</span> Cone r = 3, h = 4. Slant height and CSA?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> l = 5 → π × 3 × 5 <b>= l = 5, 15π ≈ 47.1</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">42.</span> Sphere radius 3. Volume and surface?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> ⁴⁄₃π27 · 4π9 <b>= 36π ≈ 113.1, 36π</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">43.</span> How many 2 cm cubes fit in a 10 × 8 × 6 cm box?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> 5 × 4 × 3 <b>= 60</b></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#c62828\">44.</span> Wire 44 cm bent into a circle (π = 22/7). Area enclosed?</p><p><span style=\"color:#1565c0\">▸</span> r = 44/(2π) = 7 → πr² <b>= 154 cm²</b></p></div>",[]]}